    watchdog autofix: UNTRACKED_MONEY
    
    sweep() never re-read payments the desk had marked CANCELLED, so a transfer that Airwallex later paid stayed 'CANCELLED' with no alarm. Add the cancelled-payment re-read that cancel_watch was meant for: recent CANCELLED payments are re-read read-only, and _set then raises CANCELLED_THEN_PAID / CANCELLED_BUT_LIVE / CANCELLED_LOCALLY_BUT_EXISTS and freezes the incident.
    
    Gates: {"G1_G2": "G1/G2 ok", "G3_tests": "pass (no test that passed before fails now)", "G4_replays": "pass (UNTRACKED_MONEY-1448168a.json fixed; open findings 3 -> 0)", "G5_hunt": "pass (300 fresh scenarios, no new kind of break)", "G6_second_opinion": "APPROVE: The diff only adds a loop that calls the existing `reconcile()` on recent CANCELLED payments, the same pattern the PAID loop already uses, and it adds no new send, retry, or cap path. It cannot weaken an existing refusal or alarm. This assumes `reconcile()` is read-only for CANCELLED rows a"}

